  "title": "Crostata di visciole",
  "subtitle": "Roman Jewish sour cherry and ricotta lattice tart",
  "excerpt": "Crostata di visciole is a traditional Jewish-Roman tart made on the Sabbath when dairy and meat cannot be served together. A sweet, lemony shortcrust case holds a layer of sour cherry jam, covered with a smooth ricotta filling sweetened with sugar and scented with lemon, then finished with a pastry lattice. Visciole (morello-type sour cherries) give the distinctive tartness, but a good-quality sour cherry preserve gives the same result.",
