        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the pasta frolla"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Combine {{plain-flour}}, {{icing-sugar}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} in a bowl. Rub in {{unsalted-butter}} until the mixture resembles coarse sand. Add the 2 egg yolks (from {{eggs}}), the zest of {{lemon}}, and {{vanilla-extract}}, and press together until the dough just coheres. Divide into two portions, one slightly larger than the other (two-thirds and one-third). Flatten each into a disc, wrap, and refrigerate for 1 hour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Line the tin"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 180°C (conventional). Grease a 24 cm loose-bottomed tart tin. Roll the larger disc of pastry on a lightly floured surface and line the tin, pressing the pastry gently up the sides. Trim any overhang. Refrigerate while you make the filling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the ricotta filling"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beat {{ricotta}} with {{caster-sugar}}, {{eggs}}, and the zest of the second {{lemon}} until smooth. The filling should be spreadable and just pourable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fill and top with lattice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spread {{raspberry-jam}} evenly over the chilled pastry base. Pour the ricotta filling over the jam and smooth level. Roll the remaining pastry disc to a rectangle and cut into strips about 1 cm wide. Arrange in a lattice over the top of the tart, pressing the ends onto the pastry rim. Bake for 45 to 50 minutes until the lattice is golden and the ricotta filling is just set; it should have a slight wobble in the very centre. Cool in the tin for 30 minutes before unmoulding. Serve at room temperature or just slightly warm."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
